        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=14$",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras’ theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}(x-2)^2+9^2&=(x+1)^2\\\\x^2-4x+85&=x^2+2x+1\\\\6x&=84\\\\x&=14.\\end{align*}$$\nThe side lengths are $12$, $9$ and $15$, all positive.",
